{
 "translation": "But among the women Miss Sarabhai brought in the military truck for transfer, Lajo was not there. Sundarlal, with hope and fear, watched the last girl get down from the truck, and then he quietly and with great determination doubled his committee's activities. Now, he would not only go out for the morning procession but also organize processions in the evening, and sometimes even hold small gatherings, in which the committee's old president, lawyer Kalkaprasad Sufi, would give a speech mixed with abuses, and Salu would always be present on duty with a spittoon. Strange noises would come from the loudspeaker. Then, somewhere, Nekiram Muharrir of the police station would get up to say something, but the more things he said and the more scriptures and Puranas he cited, the more he spoke against his own objective. And seeing the field slipping from his hands, Sundarlal Babu would get up, but he could not say anything beyond two sentences. His throat would choke up. Tears would start flowing from his eyes, and because of becoming tearful, he couldn't give the speech. Finally, he would sit down. But a strange kind of silence would fall upon the crowd, and the effect of Sundarlal Babu's two words, which came from the depths of his heart, would outweigh all the eloquent advice of lawyer Kalkaprasad Sufi. But people would cry right there, satisfy their emotions, and then return home with empty minds.",
